## API Reference

| Prop | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `children` | `ReactNode` | Components to protect |
| `fallback` | `ReactNode \| (props: FallbackProps) => ReactNode` | Custom fallback UI or render prop |
| `onError` | `(log: ErrorLog) => void` | Callback fired on each error (use for Sentry, etc.) |
| `onReset` | `() => void` | Callback fired when boundary resets |
| `resetKeys` | `unknown[]` | Changing any key auto-resets the boundary |
| `isolate` | `boolean` | Wraps children in a `<div>` to contain layout impact |

### Key Design Decisions

- **`getDerivedStateFromError`** handles the render-phase state update (pure, no side effects)
- **`componentDidCatch`** handles side effects — logging, callbacks, incrementing error count
- **`resetKeys`** enables parent-driven recovery without prop drilling a reset function
- **`ErrorLogger`** is a static singleton so logs persist across boundary resets for debugging
- The **render prop pattern** for `fallback` gives consumers full control over the error UI while still receiving typed `FallbackProps`
